<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{{title}} — Nimbus</title>
    <style>
        :root { --mono: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; --sans: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
                --bg: #e8eaed; --surface: #fafbfc; --line: #d2d7de; --ink: #1b2027; --ink-2: #5a626d;
                --ok: #1f6b4a; --ok-soft: #e0efe7; --fault: #a32c22; --fault-soft: #f7e3e1; --accent: #97671a; }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; }
        body { font-family: var(--sans); background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }
        main { max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2rem; }
        .badge { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .75rem; padding: .2rem .6rem; border-radius: 3px; }
        .badge.ok { background: var(--ok-soft); color: var(--ok); }
        .badge.denied { background: var(--fault-soft); color: var(--fault); }
        h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: .75rem 0 1.25rem; }
        p { color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
        ol { color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.25rem; }
        code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .85em; }
        nav a { color: var(--accent); margin-right: 1rem; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    {{#denied}}
    <span class="badge denied">403 — role missing</span>
    <h1>{{title}}</h1>
    <p>You are signed in as <code>{{username}}</code>, but this page requires
       the <code>admin</code> realm role and your session carries
       {{#has_roles}}only: {{#roles}}<code>{{name}}</code> {{/roles}}{{/has_roles}}
       {{^has_roles}}no realm roles at all{{/has_roles}}.</p>
    <p>That is the demonstration: authentication and authorization are
       separate checks. To grant the role:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Open the Keycloak admin console{{#admin_console}} at <code>{{admin_console}}</code>{{/admin_console}}
            (credentials: <code>composer nimbus:vault-view</code>)</li>
        <li>Realm <code>{{realm}}</code> → Users → <code>{{username}}</code> → Role mapping</li>
        <li>Assign <code>admin</code>, then sign out and back in so the new
            role lands in a fresh token</li>
    </ol>
    {{/denied}}
    {{^denied}}
    <span class="badge ok">signed in — admin role</span>
    <h1>{{title}}</h1>
    <p>You are seeing this because your token carries the <code>admin</code>
       realm role. This is where an app would put its dangerous buttons.</p>
    {{/denied}}

    <nav>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/protected">/protected</a>
        <a href="/auth/logout?redirect=/">Sign out</a>
    </nav>
</main>
</body>
</html>
